# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Modified:** `package.json`
  - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0 to dependencies

- **Modified:** `package-lock.json`
  - Updated lock file with new dependency tree (647 packages added during installation)

### 2. Component Integration
- **Modified:** `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag of the root layout
  - Reformatted body structure for better readability (preserved all existing functionality)

## Implementation Details

**Framework:** Next.js v16.3.8 (App Router)

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation for Next.js v13.5+:
- Used the Next.js-specific package import: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the component in the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) to ensure tracking across all pages
- The component was added at the end of the body tag, after existing components, to avoid interfering with the app's functionality

## Verification

✅ **Package Installation:** Successfully installed via npm
✅ **Linter:** No new linting errors introduced in modified files
✅ **Code Structure:** Preserved all existing functionality and imports
✅ **TypeScript:** Changes follow proper TypeScript conventions

**Note:** The build command encountered pre-existing TypeScript errors related to Prisma type generation (unrelated to Speed Insights changes). The Speed Insights integration itself is properly implemented and will work correctly once the Prisma-related issues are resolved.

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
3. No additional configuration is required - the tracking script deploys automatically with the application

## Dependencies

The Speed Insights component will track Web Vitals metrics including:
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- First Input Delay (FID)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)
- Interaction to Next Paint (INP)
